atus/2115677817820368896"}, {"author_id": "2015753413418762240", "created_at": "2026-10-28T09:47:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115379935875408354"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "ORCL"}, {"end": 11, "start": 6, "tag": "CBRS"}, {"end": 18, "start": 12, "tag": "GOOGL"}, {"end": 24, "start": 19, "tag": "NVDA"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/S26tR0UE31", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Schulz_Research/status/2115379935875408354/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115379921564672000", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/S26tR0UE31"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/S26tR0UE31", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Schulz_Research/status/2115379935875408354/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115379928921489408", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/S26tR0UE31"}]}, "id": "2115379935875408354", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 973, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "$ORCL $CBRS $GOOGL $NVDA\nOracle put three non-Nvidia chips on its cloud roadmap yesterday, and none of them comes with a volume, a price or a 2026 date. The chip customers can rent on OCI today is Nvidia's Vera Rubin, which Oracle plans to take to multi-gigawatt scale.\n\nWhat the https://t.co/S26tR0UE31", "url": "https://x.com/Schulz_Research/status/2115379935875408354"}, {"author_id": "1456593117017255939", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:39:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115211815395250621", "2115211900132684030"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "CRDO"}]}, "id": "2115211815395250621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$CRDO Why \"reliability\" is the thesis:\n\nIn an AI cluster, every GPU connects to its first network switch through one link. That link has no backup.\n\nIf it “flaps” (drops and reconnects for a split second), bad data spreads, and the training job can stall across tens of thousands", "url": "https://x.com/Caan_Pau/status/2115211815395250621"}, {"author_id": "1028566154758029313", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:04:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115489942373576711"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "1063624591", "start": 25, "username": "ONUG_"}], "urls": [{"description": "This session explores how full-stack optimization across compute, networking, and software can unlock higher GPU utilization, faster training, and more predictable performance in AMD-based AI clusters. Attendees will learn practical design principles for building high-performance Ethernet fabrics, reducing bottlenecks, and optimizing the complete AI stack, from GPU communication to cluster-scale architecture. Ideal for enterprise infrastructure leaders planning or expanding AI deployments.", "display_url": "onug.net/events/ai-netw…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "AI Networking & Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters - DriveNets Triple-T - ONUG", "unwound_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "url": "https://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/WXWBoRsy77", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2115489942373576711/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115489782159536129", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WXWBoRsy77"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/WXWBoRsy77", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2115489942373576711/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115489781991739393", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WXWBoRsy77"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/WXWBoRsy77", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2115489942373576711/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115489781928869888", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WXWBoRsy77"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/WXWBoRsy77", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2115489942373576711/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115489782029557760", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WXWBoRsy77"}]}, "id": "2115489942373576711", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Come by our booth at the @ONUG_  AI Networking Summit and talk to our AI infrastructure experts - Sagie Fanish, Shai Haim, and Henrique Trevisan\n\nJoin our session!\n\n👉 AI Networking &amp; Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters\n\nOctober 29 | 2:30 pm ET\nhttps://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x\n\nIn https://t.co/WXWBoRsy77", "url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2115489942373576711"}, {"author_id": "1456593117017255939", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:39:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115211815395250621", "2115211900132684030"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "CRDO"}]}, "id": "2115211900132684030", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 255, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$CRDO Why \"reliability\" is the thesis 🧵\n\nIn an AI cluster, every GPU connects to its first network switch through one link. That link has no backup.\n\nIf it “flaps” (drops and reconnects for a split second), bad data spreads, and the training job can stall across tens of", "url": "https://x.com/Caan_Pau/status/2115211900132684030"}, {"author_id": "809836534631460864", "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:29:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115420574126313554"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "IREN"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/M3imckUztR", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ColeHarrisonFin/status/2115420574126313554/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115402977200783361", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/M3imckUztR"}]}, "id": "2115420574126313554", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 305, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$IREN: A vertically integrated AI cloud infrastructure company undergoing a complete transformation from Bitcoin mining. It owns its own land, power access, data centers, GPU computing power, and software layer, rather than simply engaging in mining or hosting. The company has https://t.co/M3imckUztR", "url": "https://x.com/ColeHarrisonFin/status/2115420574126313554"}, {"author_id": "829074236782161920", "created_at": "2026-10-28T04:21:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115297934627705241"], "id": "2115297934627705241", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 97, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oracle just revealed where the next major AI infrastructure opportunity is forming. And I don’t think it’s another GPU company.\n\nOn October 27, Oracle announced plans to bring Google TPUs to OCI in 2027, expand NVIDIA Vera Rubin capacity to multi-gigawatt scale, and add Cerebras", "url": "https://x.com/vincentinvests/status/2115297934627705241"}, {"article": {"title": "Why I’m not building a Neocloud"}, "author_id": "2034130498445041664", "created_at": "2026-10-29T13:33:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115799063085928883"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 210, "start": 193, "tag": "AIInfrastructure"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2115…", "end": 234, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115796531961888768", "start": 211, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115796531961888768", "url": "https://t.co/fyaTHtcNlS"}]}, "id": "2115799063085928883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 580, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The GPU cloud isn’t broken. Its capital structure is.\n\nOur CEO Davy Wang on why GoodVision AI isn’t building a Neocloud, and the three lessons from the first cloud war that shaped our model. \n\n#AIInfrastructure https://t.co/fyaTHtcNlS", "url": "https://x.com/GoodVisionAI/status/2115799063085928883"}, {"author_id": "1920651001327202304", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:27:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115556093279801830"], "id": "2115556093279801830", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "There was a time where your family owning a personal computer at home gave you an unmatched leg up against your peers, completely reshaping the trajectory of your life (young Mark Zuckerberg opportunity). There really hasn't been any technology since then that could give a kid", "url": "https://x.com/ryanhuos/status/2115556093279801830"}, {"author_id": "1500129839583567875", "created_at": "2026-10-29T05:47:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115682004989567011"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/PyTorch/status…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/PyTorch/status/2115501310233456900", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/mXjhMK00VT"}]}, "id": "2115682004989567011", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 47, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115501310233456900", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "After upgrading to PyTorch 2.15, every distributed NCCL training job runs on a new backend, and Macs on macOS 14 lose GPU acceleration.\n\nThe release, out yesterday, packs 3,117 commits from 583 contributors. The rewritten NCCL backend, opt-in as nccl2 in 2.14, is now the default https://t.co/mXjhMK00VT", "url": "https://x.com/MartinSzerment/status/2115682004989567011"}, {"author_id": "1808575657762566145", "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:37:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115436326623289524", "2115437919267664016"], "id": "2115437919267664016", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "LLM-written GPU kernels have a quiet failure mode: they look correct, compile fine, and return the wrong numbers. Train a model on that code and it learns the same mistakes.\n\nSo I built a data pipeline with one rule: a kernel only gets into the dataset if it proves itself.\n\nA", "url": "https://x.com/ThanaysisirA/status/2115437919267664016"}, {"author_id": "1808575657762566145", "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:31:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115436326623289524", "2115437919267664016"], "id": "2115436326623289524", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "LLM-written GPU kernels have a quiet failure mode: they look correct, compile fine, and return the wrong numbers. Train a model on that code and it learns the same mistakes.\n\nSo I built a data pipeline with one rule: a kernel only gets into the dataset if it proves itself.\n\nA", "url": "https://x.com/ThanaysisirA/status/2115436326623289524"}, {"author_id": "872609702621970433", "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:25:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115872707321430143"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 15, "start": 7, "tag": "AItrade"}, {"end": 76, "start": 67, "tag": "Earnings"}, {"end": 101, "start": 92, "tag": "AIStocks"}], "urls": [{"description": "🚨 InvestingPro - 55% + AN EXTRA 15% WITH MY CODE 👉 Subscribe here:...", "display_url": "youtu.be/eUiiYCApaBA", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://youtu.be/eUiiYCApaBA", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115828317538390016/0mmlpPkg?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115828317